From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:04:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: novatek-nt36523: Add Lenovo Legion Y700 (2025)
 panels

The Lenovo Legion Y700 (2025) / TB321FU has a 1600x2560 NT36523 panel
from either BOE or CSOT. Each half of the panel is driven by its own
C-PHY DSI link with three trios, and the video stream is compressed with
DSC 1.1, one 800x20 slice per link at 8 bits per pixel.

Add DSC support to the driver, and add both panels with their 120 Hz
mode and the init and off sequences of the vendor device tree.

Take the optional vdd and vci supplies and enable them after vddio in
prepare, before the reset. Boards that do not describe them get dummy
regulators.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig                 |   2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c | 296 +++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 296 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

